{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And behold, the rams.</b> Even though Laban separated all of them so that the flock would not mate with their kind, the angels would bring them from the flock entrusted into the hand of Laban's sons to the flock in Jacob's hand (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And ringed.</b> As the Targum renders: וּפַצִּיחִין; פייש״יר בְּלַעַ״ז — a white thread encircling its body all around, its bands open and split from one to the other. And one should not bring proof from Scripture."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French pechiere, a type of streaked marking; Rashi's final remark warns against forcing a similar sense of ברד from other biblical verses."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:27.129623217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}